From bcff45f4c6bc18bf71ddc573818667d68b155d66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 07:47:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Redesign the buyer portal: modern UI, unified agent-waiting
 flow, global capability search, and a real caching fix
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Visual: editorial display font, hero-glow/noise treatments, route-level page
transitions, a pipeline tracker on the dashboard, and an activity feed —
the portal now reads as a designed product instead of a bare admin panel.

Fixes the reported "data gets cached" bug at its actual root cause: the
buyer layout read localStorage once in its render body and never noticed
buyerId/companyName appearing mid-session (nothing to do with fetch
caching, which was already correct everywhere). Replaced with a reactive
useBuyerSession() hook, and disabled the App Router's client-side route
staleTime so navigating back to a page always remounts fresh.

Unifies five different scattered "waiting for the agent" visual patterns
(ad-hoc spinners, static amber cards, full-page loaders) into one
AgentWaitingState component, used consistently across discover, vendors,
solution, scenarios, and handoff. After a short delay it offers an
interactive canvas mini-game (a small themed runner, in the spirit of
Chrome's offline dinosaur game) so a multi-minute agent step isn't just a
static spinner.

Adds a real "search by capability" feature: a header command-palette
(Cmd/Ctrl+K) searching every published vendor's full Solution DNA, not
just the buyer's own recommendation list, which was the only capability
search that existed before.

Adds deck/run history: previous pitch-deck versions on the solution
workspace, and a run activity feed on the dashboard, both backed by the
buyer_workflow_runs/buyer_solution_decks tables.
